# Automation Scope

- Three automation workstreams agreed for the project:
  1. Automated ETL pipeline: sync script via Statistics Canada REST API fetches updated vectors; lightweight scraper for CIHI database replaces manual CSV downloads; appends new data points to existing files
  2. Data quality assurance: automated validation layer for suppression codes, missing values, and duplicate entries; addresses bugs that caused prior issues in the pipeline
  3. MCP server: lightweight Python server exposing read-only SQL tools (e.g., get_provincial_KPI, run_sql_query, get_gender_paradox_stats); any connected LLM can answer natural-language questions against the data without hallucination
- Papermill orchestrator also scoped: single script runs all six notebooks end-to-end, logs memory usage and execution time, can be triggered locally or via GitHub Actions
  - Agreed it can be written and documented even if not fully deployed in production
- Automated relational database rebuild also discussed: recreates the unified SQLite database from raw data on demand; solves the in-memory database problem where data is lost when notebooks close
- Philip to decide between prioritizing SQL automation or MCP server first; README with automation steps already pushed to the repo
- MCP server seen as the highest-impact demo item: plan to connect it to Ollama locally and run live queries during the presentation

